Cuboidz wrote:

> I'm pretty new to Nethack, and I've come to dislike shops because of
> all the drudgery involved in putting them to good use: price-ID'ing
> scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...

> So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> encounter a shop?

I usually let them be, until I have food to spare. But then, I go for 
the full Monty (provided I have a pet).

First, I follow my pet into the shop and look where he's walking. I 
trace his steps to pick up all uncursed items (save for scrolls), and 
drop those on several stacks near the door.

Then, I locate the uncursed scrolls and kick them in the direction of 
the door, if possible. I don't pick them up to avoid being charged for a 
scroll of scare monster I might accidentally destroy.

Next, I try to detect the mimics by throwing things at the remaining 
items and kill them. If I guess I'm not strong enough, I just leave the 
shop and come back, after which they will be hiding again.

The non-mimics that are left are cursed objects. I try to arrange those 
(and the ones I am carrying myself) in a straight line crossing the 
shop, to prevent my pet picking up objects near the door, and dropping 
them somewhere in the back of the shop.

Then I wait, one square outside the shop, for my pet to drop items in my 
lap. If I have a fair amount of gold, I drop it inside the shop as well, 
and repeat that if my pet brings it to me.

Finally, after I've cleared out most items, I use them to credit clone.

